-- title:
--   First inequality for cyclic extensions, with base-change datum
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ a $K$-algebra, the extension Galois with cyclic Galois group $L \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[K]} L$. The assertion is the existence of a datum $B$ of type `AdeleBaseChange (𝓞 K) K (𝓞 L) L`, that is: a ring homomorphism $\beta \colon \mathbb{A}_K \to \mathbb{A}_L$ between the adele rings, compatible with the diagonal embeddings in the sense that $\beta(\iota_K(e)) = \iota_L(e)$ for every $e \in K$ (where $e$ on the right is viewed in $L$), together with an isomorphism of $\mathbb{A}_K$-algebras $\mathbb{A}_K \otimes_K L \cong \mathbb{A}_L$ ($\mathbb{A}_L$ being an $\mathbb{A}_K$-algebra via $\beta$) carrying $1 \otimes l$ to $\iota_L(l)$ for all $l \in L$, such that the subgroup of $\mathbb{A}_K^\times$ generated by `principalIdeles (𝓞 K) K`, the image of $K^\times$ under the diagonal map, together with the range of `B.idelicNorm`, the map induced on unit groups by the algebra norm $\mathbb{A}_L \to \mathbb{A}_K$ attached to $\beta$, has index in $\mathbb{A}_K^\times$ that is nonzero as a natural number (that is, finite) and divisible by $\operatorname{finrank}_K L = [L:K]$.
--
--   This is the first inequality of global class field theory in Chevalley's idelic form, for a cyclic extension of number fields: the norm coset subgroup $K^\times \cdot N_{L/K}(\mathbb{A}_L^\times)$ has finite index divisible by the degree. It is used to obtain the corresponding statement for an arbitrary base-change datum, in [`M4aHerbrand.ideleClass_normCoset_index_ne_zero_and_finrank_dvd`](thm.html#M4aHerbrand.ideleClass_normCoset_index_ne_zero_and_finrank_dvd), the index and the norm image being independent of the choice of $B$.
